[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2736023357","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/104337#issuecomment-2736023357","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/104337","id":2736023357,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6jFGc9","user":{"login":"Grublady","id":29121925,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI5MTIxOTI1","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/29121925?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Grublady","html_url":"https://github.com/Grublady","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Grublady/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Grublady/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Grublady/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Grublady/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Grublady/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Grublady/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Grublady/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Grublady/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Grublady/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-03-19T10:07:37Z","updated_at":"2025-03-19T10:07:37Z","body":"Reproducible on macOS 15.3, however I was able to reproduce on 4.4dev3 and even 4.3 as well.\n\nIt is more noticeable starting in dev4, which I'd wager is due to #98131 no longer falsely \"covering it up\" with a fade.\n\nEither way, I don't think the issue at hand is a recent regression.\n\nIt also seems to be unrelated to bus effects, as I was able to reproduce the issue even with the effects removed.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2736023357/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2736541427","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/104337#issuecomment-2736541427","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/104337","id":2736541427,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6jHE7z","user":{"login":"TheWoodenTree","id":94566175,"node_id":"U_kgDOBaL3Hw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/94566175?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheWoodenTree","html_url":"https://github.com/TheWoodenTree","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheWoodenTree/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheWoodenTree/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheWoodenTree/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheWoodenTree/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheWoodenTree/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheWoodenTree/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheWoodenTree/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheWoodenTree/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheWoodenTree/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-03-19T12:56:33Z","updated_at":"2025-03-19T12:57:41Z","body":"That's strange. Did you just remove the Area3D? I am unable to hear the issue when the Area3D is removed or the audio player directly has its bus set to the new bus with reverb. I tried this on macOS 14.5. \n\nAlso this appears to be related to #103776, though adding fade-in did not appear to entirely fix the issue, but it did lessen it slightly. I'm not very familiar with audio, so perhaps I'm not adding enough, but I feel like fading in the first 0.1 seconds would have made it unnoticeable. I'm also not sure why I need the conditions I have to reproduce the issue on my end, or at least to a degree that is noticeable to my ears.","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2736541427/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2737420307","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/104337#issuecomment-2737420307","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/104337","id":2737420307,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6jKbgT","user":{"login":"Calinou","id":180032,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE4MDAzMg==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/180032?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou","html_url":"https://github.com/Calinou","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-03-19T17:05:17Z","updated_at":"2025-03-19T17:05:28Z","body":"Area-based audio bus effects need some form of fading to avoid pop-in (but also to sound less jarring). This should probably use a custom system where you specify a fade duration in seconds, either on a per-Area3D basis or as a project setting (it could default to something like `0.25` seconds).","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2737420307/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2737570687","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/104337#issuecomment-2737570687","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/104337","id":2737570687,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6jLAN_","user":{"login":"Grublady","id":29121925,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI5MTIxOTI1","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/29121925?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Grublady","html_url":"https://github.com/Grublady","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Grublady/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Grublady/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Grublady/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Grublady/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Grublady/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Grublady/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Grublady/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Grublady/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Grublady/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-03-19T18:01:57Z","updated_at":"2025-03-19T18:01:57Z","body":"> That's strange. Did you just remove the Area3D?\n\nWhat I mean is that the `Reverb` and `Amplify` can be removed from the audio buses and the pop still occurs.\n\n> Also this appears to be related to https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/103776, though adding fade-in did not appear to entirely fix the issue, but it did lessen it slightly.\n\nThe issue here looks to be related to the bus routing, not the sample itself as in #103776.\n(Note how there is no pop when routing directly to a bus, but there is one when using an `Area3D`'s reverb send, even with the very same stream.)\n\n> Area-based audio bus effects need some form of fading to avoid pop-in (but also to sound less jarring).\n\nAny need for fading an area-based send would be when a stream enters or exits the area.\nIn the MRP, the `AudioStreamPlayer3D` is always inside the area, so this is an orthogonal concern.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2737570687/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5177127498","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/104337#issuecomment-5177127498","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/104337","id":5177127498,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABNJSySg","user":{"login":"Jaytheway","id":22476284,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIyNDc2Mjg0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/22476284?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jaytheway","html_url":"https://github.com/Jaytheway","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jaytheway/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jaytheway/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jaytheway/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jaytheway/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jaytheway/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jaytheway/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jaytheway/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jaytheway/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jaytheway/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-08-04T09:27:49Z","updated_at":"2026-08-04T09:27:49Z","body":"It's hard to validate that the issue has anything to do with reverb, or amplifier on a master bus.\n\nThe PR (#104382) seems to be addressing _a_ problem. However, I suspect the root cause is lack of fades when buses change, as in #104833.\n\nI suggest reevaluating this issue after #104833 has been addressed.","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5177127498/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null}]